WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.891
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Wednesday, October twenty first.

2
00:00:04.891 --> 00:00:12.324
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.324 --> 00:00:15.424
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.424 --> 00:00:16.931
We start in Nigeria.

5
00:00:16.931 --> 00:00:25.639
The World Health Organization says Nigeria has confirmed one imported case of Bundibugyo virus disease, a form of Ebola, in the Federal Capital Territory around Abuja.

6
00:00:25.639 --> 00:00:32.449
Nigeria is the fifth country to detect the virus since the outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo was declared in May.

7
00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:38.161
The patient is a woman who recently travelled from Uganda, and forty four contacts are being monitored.

8
00:00:38.161 --> 00:00:47.460
The WHO advises against travel or trade restrictions, and the State Department travel account says health officials are conducting contact tracing.

9
00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:56.293
In Mali, Reuters, in a report shared by ACLED, says at least forty eight civilians were killed in eastern Mali in attacks attributed to Islamic State linked militants.

10
00:00:56.293 --> 00:01:05.747
ACLED data show clashes between the Islamic State Sahel Province and al Qaeda affiliates have left more than two thousand dead since twenty nineteen.

11
00:01:05.747 --> 00:01:16.325
In Sudan, BBC Africa reports the army has been accused of launching several drone strikes that reportedly killed more than two hundred people, including dozens travelling to a funeral.

12
00:01:16.325 --> 00:01:29.573
In Ethiopia, the Critical Threats Project says the Tigray People's Liberation Front warned the federal government against using airports for military purposes, and threatened to shoot down Ethiopian Airlines planes carrying suspected military equipment and personnel.

13
00:01:29.573 --> 00:01:36.300
Federal forces are reportedly redeploying from the Eritrean border toward the Tigrayan cities of Adwa and Adigrat.

14
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:43.656
The UN humanitarian office says renewed fighting is making an already dire humanitarian situation worse.

15
00:01:43.656 --> 00:01:48.967
In Italy, the State Department travel account says protests may occur across the country over the next few days.

16
00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:58.397
Recent demonstrations in Milan and Bologna led to looting and violent clashes, and more demonstrators may gather in city center squares and near main railway stations.

17
00:01:58.397 --> 00:02:10.089
Australia says even peaceful demonstrations can escalate quickly, and the UK Foreign Office has added information about a national strike planned for October thirtieth.

18
00:02:10.089 --> 00:02:11.638
A few updates on stories we've covered.

19
00:02:11.638 --> 00:02:23.296
On Ebola in Kenya, BBC Africa reports Kenya has now confirmed nine cases linked to one man who travelled from Congo through Uganda, and a doctors' union warns of understaffed border crossings.

20
00:02:23.296 --> 00:02:35.385
On Saudi Arabia, the State Department travel account says US government employees there need special authorization to use any airport in the country, and reminds US citizens to follow Saudi Civil Defense alerts sent by cellular broadcast.

21
00:02:35.385 --> 00:02:46.610
Dawn reports the Saudi led coalition said it intercepted a Houthi ballistic missile targeting Riyadh, and that the UK will deploy Typhoon fighter jets to defend Saudi cities.

22
00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:56.911
Update on Yemen: the Critical Threats Project and the Institute for the Study of War say Houthi and government-aligned forces are likely still contesting Jabal Han, a mountain overlooking western Taiz City.

23
00:02:56.911 --> 00:03:04.024
The Houthis likely fired several ballistic missiles at Marib City on October nineteenth.

24
00:03:04.024 --> 00:03:06.067
Now a few quick notes by region.

25
00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:16.501
In the Middle East and North Africa, Reuters reports Iraq has closed the Sheeb border crossing with Iran to passengers, vehicles and commercial trucks until further notice.

26
00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:22.606
Long War Journal reports Iran says it has an agreement with Iraq to expel Kurdish Iranian opposition groups.

27
00:03:22.606 --> 00:03:28.448
And Reuters says Turkey is planning a mandate to send military personnel to Saudi Arabia.

28
00:03:28.448 --> 00:03:37.832
In Africa, BBC Africa reports former Rwandan army sergeant major Robert Kabera, a critic of President Paul Kagame, was found beheaded in neighbouring Uganda.

29
00:03:37.832 --> 00:03:44.481
Residents near Pretoria, South Africa, have been told not to drink or cook with tap water after more than four hundred people, mostly young children, fell ill.

30
00:03:44.481 --> 00:03:52.723
And the UK Foreign Office updated its Tanzania advice on Ebola screening and the risk of protests on October twenty ninth.

31
00:03:52.723 --> 00:04:02.697
In the Americas, InSight Crime reports an attack in Croix-des-Bouquets, Haiti, a stronghold of the four hundred Mawozo gang, left four Salvadoran soldiers missing.

32
00:04:02.697 --> 00:04:08.954
In Asia Pacific, Canada is tracking Typhoon Champi, expected to sweep across the Ryukyu Islands and Okinawa in Japan.

33
00:04:08.954 --> 00:04:15.708
Reuters reports North Korea's army chief inspected the border with South Korea and said troops must act if provoked.

34
00:04:15.708 --> 00:04:22.846
And Australian lawmaker Helen Haines had both legs amputated after being rammed by a car outside her electoral office.

35
00:04:22.846 --> 00:04:25.713
The accused has appeared in court.

36
00:04:25.713 --> 00:04:37.900
In Europe, the Institute for the Study of War cites Ukraine's prime minister saying a Russian strike on a park in Nova Vodolaha, in Kharkiv province, killed at least six people, including two children, on October nineteenth.

37
00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:45.371
Russia launched one hundred sixty five drones at Ukraine overnight, and Reuters reports Russian drones killed two people near Kharkiv.

38
00:04:45.371 --> 00:04:51.529
In Russia, the governor of the Bryansk region says one person was killed in an attack.

39
00:04:51.529 --> 00:05:00.062
On cyber, CISA, the FBI and the Secret Service issued an advisory on SafePay ransomware targeting businesses and critical infrastructure worldwide.

40
00:05:00.062 --> 00:05:12.235
Reuters reports a cyber agency warned websites may go dark as PHP prepares a critical fix, and State Bank of India reported a cyberattack involving nearly three thousand nine hundred customer records.

41
00:05:12.235 --> 00:05:13.611
That's today's brief.

42
00:05:13.611 --> 00:05:21.712
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

43
00:05:21.712 --> 00:05:29.880
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

44
00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.940
This brief is digitally narrated.

45
00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:32.881
Questions?

46
00:05:32.881 --> 00:05:36.414
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

47
00:05:36.414 --> 00:05:38.419
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
